WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.221 --> 00:00:15.909
[g@"This is ridiculous," said the Tang Monk.

2
00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:21.933
"Why are we under arrest?"@g] Soldiers were bringing the travelers back to the town.

3
00:00:21.953 --> 00:00:27.256
"You robbed Squire Kou's house last night," said one of the soldiers.

4
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.261
[g@"What!" cried Bajie.

5
00:00:30.281 --> 00:00:36.445
"We would never rob somebody.@g] Especially not the squire—he was kind to us!"

6
00:00:37.505 --> 00:00:40.707
"You had all the stolen items," replied the soldier.

7
00:00:40.727 --> 00:00:44.709
"You also had the two horses that were stolen from his stable."

8
00:00:44.729 --> 00:00:48.611
"We got everything from the real robbers," said the Tang Monk.

9
00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:52.293
"We were going to return it all to Squire Kou!"

10
00:00:52.313 --> 00:00:55.535
[g@The soldier laughed.

11
00:00:56.156 --> 00:01:02.830
"Oh? You got everything from the [i@real@i] robbers?@g] Tell me, where are the [i@real@i] robbers now?

12
00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.550
Hmm?" [g@Wukong sighed.

13
00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:10.752
"I let them go."@g] [g@The soldier laughed again.

14
00:01:10.772 --> 00:01:17.514
"Oh, that was very kind of you!"@g] Wukong could tell that the soldier didn't believe him.

15
00:01:17.514 --> 00:01:22.895
[g@By now they had reached the town.

16
00:01:23.735 --> 00:01:30.734
A crowd of people had gathered to watch.@g] The soldiers brought the travelers into the courthouse.

17
00:01:30.754 --> 00:01:33.956
[g@The judge frowned at the monk and the others.

18
00:01:33.976 --> 00:01:39.480
"Lock them up!"@g] "This is a mistake," the Tang Monk pleaded.

19
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.662
[g@"We can't go to jail.

20
00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:47.206
We're making an important journey to visit Buddha."@g] The judge shook his head.

21
00:01:47.226 --> 00:01:50.688
"Buddha doesn't allow killers in the Western Paradise."

22
00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:53.751
[g@"Killers?" said Wujing.

23
00:01:53.771 --> 00:01:59.409
"What are you talking about?"@g] "You killed Squire Kou," said the judge.

24
00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:02.170
[g@The Tang Monk's face went pale.

25
00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.752
"The squire is dead?"@g] [g@The judge narrowed his eyes at the monk.

26
00:02:06.772 --> 00:02:17.197
"Yes. And Lady Kou saw you do it."@g] The travelers were shoved into a jail cell, and the

27
00:02:17.277 --> 00:02:18.837
door was slammed shut.

28
00:02:18.857 --> 00:02:21.918
[g@The Tang Monk started to cry.

29
00:02:21.938 --> 00:02:28.631
"This is terrible!"@g] [g@Bajie made a fist.

30
00:02:28.651 --> 00:02:34.356
"Lady Kou framed us!"@g] [g@"Yes," said Wujing, nodding.

31
00:02:34.376 --> 00:02:40.781
"But why?"@g] "I'll find out tonight," promised Wukong.

32
00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.783
[g@"Thank you, Wukong."

33
00:02:43.043 --> 00:02:47.247
The Tang Monk looked grateful.@g] "We must prove our innocence!"

34
00:02:49.729 --> 00:02:55.778
That night Wukong turned into a bee and flew out of the jail and to Squire Kou's house.

35
00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:01.141
He found Lady Kou mourning over a coffin.

36
00:03:03.002 --> 00:03:06.904
The monkey changed back into himself and hid behind a curtain.

37
00:03:06.924 --> 00:03:11.287
[g@Imitating the squire's voice, he said, "My lady!

38
00:03:11.887 --> 00:03:16.330
It's me, your husband."@g] [g@Lady Kou's eyes went wide.

39
00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:22.709
"Husband? Is it really you?"@g] "Yes," said Wukong.

40
00:03:22.729 --> 00:03:26.972
"Why did you tell the judge that the Tang Monk and his companions killed me?"

41
00:03:26.992 --> 00:03:29.194
[g@Lady Kou hesitated.

42
00:03:29.214 --> 00:03:36.839
"I I was angry with them.@g] You wanted them to stay here, but they insisted on leaving.

43
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.581
That was an insult to us."

44
00:03:41.642 --> 00:03:43.584
"You have done a terrible thing!"

45
00:03:43.604 --> 00:03:44.785
thundered Wukong.

46
00:03:45.865 --> 00:03:49.268
The walls of the house shook, and Lady Kou trembled.

47
00:03:50.284 --> 00:03:51.525
The monkey continued.

48
00:03:51.545 --> 00:03:56.487
"Tomorrow you must tell the judge that the Tang Monk and his companions are innocent.

49
00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:00.989
If you don't, I will haunt you for the rest of your life!"

50
00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.791
Tears poured from the woman's eyes.

51
00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:10.013
[g@"I will talk to the judge tomorrow, I promise.

52
00:04:10.673 --> 00:04:16.376
Please don't haunt me!"@g] Wukong flew back to the courthouse.

53
00:04:17.748 --> 00:04:20.750
He saw the judge sitting at a desk, reading some papers.

54
00:04:21.891 --> 00:04:23.632
Wukong flew over the roof.

55
00:04:27.755 --> 00:04:31.757
Then he turned into an enormous spirit body and lowered one foot.

56
00:04:33.438 --> 00:04:36.501
When the judge saw the giant foot, he gasped.

57
00:04:37.481 --> 00:04:39.002
The papers fell from his hands.

58
00:04:40.043 --> 00:04:41.684
Wukong's voice boomed.

59
00:04:41.704 --> 00:04:47.548
"I am the Wandering Spirit, and I was sent here by Buddha.

60
00:04:48.872 --> 00:04:54.177
Lady Kou lied to you—the Tang Monk didn't kill Squire Kou.

61
00:04:55.238 --> 00:04:57.420
The monk is on an important journey.

62
00:04:58.782 --> 00:05:03.206
If you don't free him and his companions, I will lower my other foot.

63
00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:09.392
Then I will stomp all over this town until there is nothing left!"
